{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS2LEyy9y3Fb8mV11mF7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The job did run every night. It failed each time, and it couldn't send a message about the failure. Your `launchctl-print.txt` shows 6 runs, all ending with exit code 1, and the error log has the same two lines for every run. That gives two causes, both now fixed:\n\n1. **`claude` isn't logged in when launchd runs it.** The plist only sets `PATH`, so `USER` is missing and the CLI can't find your keychain login. It quits with \"Not logged in\" before doing any review. I added `USER=vk` and `HOME=/Users/vk` to the plist.\n2. **`status=$?` kills the script before it can notify you.** In zsh, `status` is read-only, so that line ends the script right after the failure and before either Telegram call. That's why you got nothing, not even a failure note. It's now `rc=$?`.\n\nI also made the next failure harder to miss:\n- An empty review now counts as a failure, even if `claude` exits 0.\n- Every message is also written to the `.err` log with a timestamp, and so is a failure of `notify.sh` itself.\n- Each run logs how long it took, so a review that ends in seconds stands out.\n- The prompt is now passed through stdin.\n- `notify.sh` now uses `curl --fail`, so a Telegram error no longer looks like success.\n\nI only tested this locally, with fake `claude` and notifier scripts. The failure, empty-output and success cases each sent the right message, and the plist passes `plutil -lint`. I didn't touch the real launchd job or Telegram, since this folder is a snapshot. The commands to reload and check it on your Mac are at the end of `ANSWER.md`. Run those, confirm a Telegram summary arrives, then break the script once on purpose to confirm the failure note arrives too.\n\nFrom your colleague's note, these parts applied directly: checking `launchctl print` and the error log first, the read-only `status` variable, and setting `USER`. Two didn't apply: there was no \"Input must be provided\" error, and `< /dev/null` wasn't needed. `ANSWER.md` has the full breakdown.\n\nFiles changed:\n- `bin/nightly-review.zsh`\n- `bin/notify.sh`\n- `Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist`\n- `ANSWER.md` (new)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1747,"cache_read_input_tokens":27794,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1747},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cbbb45f1-0f78-40da-aad6-56eef900731a","uuid":"93b0e7cc-ad11-4054-bc9b-2d629c8cd929","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:22:22.014Z","request_id":"req_011CgS2LE7cnXUb2cmEkdoKC"}
